# Transcripts (crates/infrastructure/src/claude/transcript.rs)

Shared by every agent's reader: `jsonl.rs` (`Follow` for incremental reads of complete lines,
`head_lines`, `tail_lines`, `parse_iso_ms`, `local_day`, `cap`) and `tools.rs` (one-line tool labels).
Codex's rollouts → `codex.mdc`. The service picks the reader by the session's provider (`AgentPorts`).

Hooks say *what state* a session is in; transcripts say *what it did*. Everything read here is
derived, recomputed and never persisted (it also works for sessions opened before the app).

## Where they are

`~/.claude/projects/<cwd-slug>/<session>.jsonl` (path comes in every hook as `transcript_path`).
Subagents: `<session>/subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl` + `agent-<id>.meta.json` (`description`,
`agentType`). The `<id>` matches the hook's `agent_id`.

## How it is read

- `read()` is **incremental**: a `Tail` per file keeps the byte offset and the facts; only complete
  lines are consumed (the last one may be half-written). First read covers the whole file up to
  64 MB (token totals must be complete), later reads cost ~0.1 ms.
- `recent()` / `subagent()` / `touched_files()` are on-demand full or tail scans (preview panel,
  changes button). Never call them on the tick.
- The first prompt comes from the head (cached per file); `ai-title` / `custom-title` /
  `last-prompt` repeat often, so the tail is enough for them.

## Trigger table

| If you… | Read |
|---|---|
| parse a new entry type or field, or a value looks wrong for a real session | `transcripts-format.md` |
| touch token counting, cost, context window or the price table | `transcripts-usage.md` |

## Invariants

- Entries with `isSidechain` belong to subagents: skip them in the main timeline, read them in the
  subagent file.
- Keep replies as Markdown (no whitespace collapsing); cap at 20 000 chars.
- An agent id ends up in a path: validate it (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]`) before joining.
